T:What it is
T:Geometry is
T:a branch of
T:math
T:concerned
T:with
T:properties
T:of space
T:such as the
T:distance,
T:shape, size,
T:and relative
T:position of
T:figures.
T:Geometry is,
T:along with
T:arithmetic,
T:one of the
T:oldest
T:branches of
T:math. A
T:mathematicia
T:who works in
T:the field of
T:geometry is
T:called a
T:geometer.
T:Until the
T:19th
T:century,
T:geometry was
T:almost
T:exclusively
T:devoted to
T:Euclidean
T:geometry,
T:which
T:includes the
T:notions of
T:point, line,
T:plane,
T:distance,
T:angle,
T:surface, and
T:curve, as
T:fundamental
T:concepts.
